    "detailedExplanationEn": "🎯 Correct Answer: Option A (\"Confirmation of apartment viewing in Ottawa this Thursday at 13h00\")\n\n• Acoustic Evidence:\nIn response to \"Why is the person leaving this phone message?\", the voicemail states: \"Real estate agency confirms apartment viewing this Thursday at 13:00 AM.\".\nOption A (\"Confirmation of apartment viewing in Ottawa this Thursday at 13h00\") accurately reflects the verified purpose in the recording.\n\n• Detailed Distractor Breakdown (Incorrect Options):\n  - Option A (\"Confirmation of apartment viewing in Ottawa this Thursday at 13h00\") [CORRECT]: Accurately reflects the central purpose or instruction communicated by the caller.\n  - Option B (\"Appointment cancellation because the apartment in Ottawa has already been rented\") [INCORRECT - SECONDARY DETAIL OR EXTRAPOLATION TRAP]: Focuses on a peripheral detail (\"Appointment cancellation because the apartment in Ottawa has already been rented\") rather than the primary purpose of the call.\n  - Option C (\"Increase in the monthly rent amount requested for the apartment\") [INCORRECT - SECONDARY DETAIL OR EXTRAPOLATION TRAP]: Focuses on a peripheral detail (\"Increase in the monthly rent amount requested for the apartment\") rather than the primary purpose of the call.\n  - Option D (\"Postponement of apartment viewing in Ottawa to late next month\") [INCORRECT - SECONDARY DETAIL OR EXTRAPOLATION TRAP]: Focuses on a peripheral detail (\"Postponement of apartment viewing in Ottawa to late next month\") rather than the primary purpose of the call.",
    "readingCoach": "💡 Stratégie A2 (Repérage de l'Objectif d'Appel) : Dès les premières secondes, repérez l'identité de la personne qui appelle (« Bonjour, c'est... » ou « Ici le secrétariat... ») ainsi que le verbe d'action (« je vous appelle pour... », « nous vous confirmons... »). Isolez le but premier de l'appel avant de consulter les propositions.",
    "readingCoachEn": "💡 Level A2 Listening Coach (Identifying Call Purpose): From the first few seconds, pinpoint the caller's identity (\"Hello, this is...\" or \"Here is the office...\") and the operative action verb (\"I am calling to...\", \"we confirm...\"). Isolate the primary reason for calling before looking at the choices."
