    "detailedExplanationEn": "🎯 Correct Answer: Option A (\"Confirmation of apartment viewing in Toronto this Thursday at 15h00\")\n\n• Acoustic Evidence:\nIn response to \"Why is the person leaving this phone message?\", the voicemail states: \"Real estate agency confirms apartment viewing this Thursday at 15:00 AM.\".\nOption A (\"Confirmation of apartment viewing in Toronto this Thursday at 15h00\") accurately reflects the verified purpose in the recording.\n\n• Detailed Distractor Breakdown (Incorrect Options):\n  - Option A (\"Confirmation of apartment viewing in Toronto this Thursday at 15h00\") [CORRECT]: Accurately reflects the central purpose or instruction communicated by the caller.\n  - Option B (\"Appointment cancellation because the apartment in Toronto has already been rented\") [INCORRECT - SECONDARY DETAIL OR EXTRAPOLATION TRAP]: Focuses on a peripheral detail (\"Appointment cancellation because the apartment in Toronto has already been rented\") rather than the primary purpose of the call.\n  - Option C (\"Increase in the monthly rent amount requested for the apartment\") [INCORRECT - SECONDARY DETAIL OR EXTRAPOLATION TRAP]: Focuses on a peripheral detail (\"Increase in the monthly rent amount requested for the apartment\") rather than the primary purpose of the call.\n  - Option D (\"Postponement of apartment viewing in Toronto to late next month\") [INCORRECT - SECONDARY DETAIL OR EXTRAPOLATION TRAP]: Focuses on a peripheral detail (\"Postponement of apartment viewing in Toronto to late next month\") rather than the primary purpose of the call.",
