    "detailedExplanationEn": "🎯 Correct Answer: Option A (\"Approval by 75% of Toronto citizens of new bike and bus lanes\")\n\n• Acoustic Evidence:\nThe radio report notes: \"A survey shows 75% citizen approval for bike lanes and bus transit in Toronto.\".\nOption A (\"Approval by 75% of Toronto citizens of new bike and bus lanes\") accurately reflects the dominant consensus highlighted in the recording.\n\n• Detailed Distractor Breakdown (Incorrect Options):\n  - Option A (\"Approval by 75% of Toronto citizens of new bike and bus lanes\") [CORRECT]: Faithfully summarizes the overall conclusion and consensus reported by the journalist.\n  - Option B (\"Mass rejection by Toronto residents of recent road development works\") [INCORRECT - MINORITY OPINION OR OVERSTATEMENT TRAP]: Isolates a marginal viewpoint or absolute claim (\"Mass rejection by Toronto residents of recent road development works\") at odds with the overall takeaway.\n  - Option C (\"Sharp increase in public transit fares in the city of Toronto\") [INCORRECT - MINORITY OPINION OR OVERSTATEMENT TRAP]: Isolates a marginal viewpoint or absolute claim (\"Sharp increase in public transit fares in the city of Toronto\") at odds with the overall takeaway.\n  - Option D (\"Permanent elimination of the municipal bike-share network\") [INCORRECT - MINORITY OPINION OR OVERSTATEMENT TRAP]: Isolates a marginal viewpoint or absolute claim (\"Permanent elimination of the municipal bike-share network\") at odds with the overall takeaway.",
